Proof ledger
  1. Divide by g=gcd(t,V).  Scale invariance sends a reduced witness tau0
     to tau=tau0/g for the original set.
  2. If a is not divisible by 13, tau0=a/(13t) makes the AP block
     {t,2t,...,12t} exactly 1/13-safe.
  3. It remains to choose a with ||aV/(13t)|| >= 1/14.
     When gcd(t,V)=1 and 13∤V, multiplication by V permutes Z/(13t),
     and the middle residues have size 13t-2ceil(13t/14)+1 > t,
     so one middle residue has preimage a not divisible by 13.
  4. When gcd(t,V)=1, 13|V, and t>1, the image is 13*Z/tZ; choose
     a middle residue modulo t and then a representative a mod 13t
     not divisible by 13.
  5. The exceptional reduced family {1,...,12,13m} has
     tau=m/(13m+1), giving every runner distance m/(13m+1) >= 1/14.
     Equality occurs only at m=1, the tight AP {1,...,13}.

